# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# This is not housekeeping. The CI workflow runs its steps as bash scripts on
# a Linux runner, and a `run:` block stored with CRLF arrives there with a
# trailing \r on every line -- which bash reports as `$'\r': command not
# found`. The Sigma emitter is similarly sensitive: its tests assert that
# generated regexes and Windows paths survive quoting intact, and a stray \r
# inside a rule is the kind of corruption that makes a detection silently
# match nothing rather than fail loudly.
#
# Developers on Windows still get CRLF in their working tree where their
# editor wants it; only what is stored here is normalised.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the files where the ending is load-bearing.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

# Never touched.
*.pfx   binary
*.p12   binary
*.exe   binary
*.db    binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
